In the summer of 2015, Goblin & oper.ru decided to start an online QuakeWorld FFA tournament with the main prize headphones and books authored by Goblin. A large number of people registered for the tournament, mostly old players, players from other quakes. Also, the tournament did not go unnoticed by "pros" and "semi-pros". A famous Russian player [[Meshuggah]] registered under a fakenick. Also, after several years of inactivity, [[gLAd]] emerged under a fakenick. The clear favorite was [[VVD]]. Unfortunately, not everyone showed up for the qualifying and other matches of the tournament. In any case, it was fun! Thank you.

==Format==

* '''Round 1 (64 Players):''' [[FFA]] (8 Players per group) on [[dm4]] (Fraglimit: 50, Timelimit: 15)
* '''Round 2 (32 Players):''' [[FFA]] (8 Players per group) on [[dm2]] (Fraglimit: 50, Timelimit: 15)
* '''Round 3 (16 Players):''' [[FFA]] (8 Players per group) on [[dm6]] (Fraglimit: 50, Timelimit: 15)
* '''Semi-Final (8 Players):''' [[FFA]] on [[dm3]] (Fraglimit: 0, Timelimit: 15)
* '''Small Final (4 Players):''' [[FFA]] on [[ztndm3]] (Fraglimit: 0, Timelimit: 15)
* '''Grand Final (4 Players):''' [[FFA]] on [[ztndm3]] (Fraglimit: 0, Timelimit: 15)

